0012 — records which string literals are, on some execution, the WHOLE
value of a `class=` attribute (`classAttrStrings`), so 0011 refuses a bad
animation name in one of them whatever else the literal holds.

Rebased onto 66caf4e5 (2026-10-22) and rebuilt on main's `markClass`
(#557, which marks the literals a `class` attribute holds for
`LiteralSite.inClass`) in place of a second walker. One edge differs and
is kept: the left operand of `&&` is in main's `inClass` and never in
`classAttrStrings`, because a non-empty string is truthy and the value is
always the right. Main's walk is wider than the one this patch had by the
parentheses and TS wrappers (`as`, `satisfies`, `!`), none of which changes
a value.

